# Fix Prompt for Failing Test /playwright/playwright:<startup>

## Diagnosis

The subject is the synthetic `<startup>` test: the Playwright run never
reached a test case. `tests/playwright.config.ts` declares

```ts
webServer: {
  command: 'docker compose up --build frontend',
  cwd: '..',
  url: 'http://127.0.0.1:3000',
  timeout: 300_000,
  reuseExistingServer: true,
},
use: { baseURL: 'http://127.0.0.1:3000' },
```

and `docker-compose.yaml` builds that service from `./services/frontend`.
**There is no `services/` directory in the workspace at all** — the compose
build fails, the web server never serves `http://127.0.0.1:3000`, and the
whole suite aborts at startup.

`tests/integration/frontend-home.spec.ts` (read-only) asserts:

```ts
await page.goto('/');
await expect(page.locator('h1')).toHaveText('Hello world');
```

`docs/architecture/architecture.yaml` declares service `frontend` at
`services/frontend`, language `typescript`, frameworks `next.js` + `react`,
App-Router server components by default, and a quality gate pointing at
`services/frontend/tsconfig.json`.

So the smallest production change is: create a minimal Next.js (App Router)
service at `services/frontend/` that Docker can build and that serves
`<h1>Hello world</h1>` on port 3000.

## Target

Create every file below with the **Write** tool. All paths are under
`services/*`. Do NOT touch `tests/`, `docs/`, `true-bdd/`,
