The text must be exactly `Hello world` — `toHaveText` is an exact match
(after whitespace trimming). Do not add sibling text inside the `h1`, and do
not add any other `h1` to the page: `page.locator('h1')` resolving to two
elements fails on strict-mode violation.

### Change #5: Dockerfile — what `docker compose up --build frontend` builds
**File:** `services/frontend/Dockerfile`
**Action:** Write (new file)
**Content:**
```dockerfile
FROM node:20-alpine

WORKDIR /app

COPY package.json ./
RUN npm install

COPY . .
RUN npm run build

EXPOSE 3000
CMD ["npm", "run", "start"]
```
Use `npm install`, not `npm ci` — there is no lockfile in the build context.

